quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  6,82,"Those who believe and do not mix up their belief with wrongdoing, it is they who shall have safety (in the Hereafter), and they are the (rightly) guided."
  6,83,"That was Our argument We gave to Ibrahim (Abraham) against his people. We raise in degrees whomsoever We please. Indeed, your Lord is All-Wise, All-Knowing."
  6,84,"And We bestowed upon him Ishaq (Isaac) and Ya‘qub (Jacob), and blessed all (of them) with guidance. And We had guided Nuh (Noah) before, and from his offspring, Dawud (David), Sulayman (Solomon), Ayyub (Job), Yusuf (Joseph), Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron). Thus, do We reward the virtuously excellent."
  6,85,"And (We guided) Zakariyya (Zachariah), Yahya (John), ‘Isa (Jesus) and Ilyas (Elias). All (of them) were among the righteous."
  6,86,"And (We also guided) Isma‘il (Ishmael), al-Yasa‘ (Elisha), Yunus (Jonah) and Lut (Lot). And We graced all (of them) over the nations,"
  6,87,"and from among their forefathers, their offspring and their brethren. We chose them and guided them to a straight path."
  6,88,"That is Allah’s guidance, with which He guides whomsoever He pleases among His servants. And if they were to ascribe partners (to Allah), whatever (good) they were doing would have been removed from them."
  6,89,"They are the ones whom We gave the Book, the (sound) judgement, and prophethood. So if these (pagans) disbelieve in them, We have already entrusted them to a people who will never deny them."
  6,90,"Those were the people whom Allah had guided. So, follow their (path of) guidance. Say: ‘I do not ask you any reward for it. It is nothing but a reminder for all the nations.’"
